# Request Validation (Node.js)

## Zod (Recommended)

- **Schema:** Define shape with z.object, z.string(), z.number(), etc.; optional, nullable, refine for custom rules
- **Type:** `type T = z.infer<typeof schema>`
- **Parse:** `schema.safeParse(body)`; on success use data; on failure return 400 with flattened errors (path + message)
- **Where:** Validate body, query, params at controller boundary before calling services

## Class-validator (Alternative)

- Use with DTO classes and decorators (@IsString, @IsEmail, etc.); validate with validate(dto); map errors to 400 response

## Conventions

- Validate all input at boundary; return a consistent RFC 7807 ProblemDetails response with field-level details when needed; do not trust client
- Use same schema for type and runtime; coerce where safe (e.g. query string to number)

## Anti-Patterns

- Validating only in service; inconsistent error format; no validation for query/params; trusting type without runtime check

